   "Text"], Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], Cell["5. Interpretation", 
   "Section"], Cell["The centered shift is 16(3 jrot^2+2 q1 q2 q3)/(q3(q1 \
q2+q1 q3+q2 q3)). All transformed metric coefficients have analytic \
generators at the horizon; scalar kinetic contractions, gauge-frame \
components, and F^I.F^J are finite. The horizon generator obeys \
chi^2=chi.eta=d_x chi^2=0 through first order, while Omega_H^(1)=0 and \
kappa^(1)=0. Coordinate logarithms are the standard ingoing-coordinate logs; \
any radial gauge-potential logarithm is locally pure gauge and does not occur \
in F^I or its invariants.", "Text"], 
  Cell["6. Remaining field-map qualification", "Section"], 
